+/// True when offsetting the faces of \a shape by \a offset (negative = towards the material) would
+/// shrink a convex cylinder, sphere or torus tube (or, for a positive offset, a concave one) to zero
+/// or negative radius. Such a face must disappear from the true offset, a topology change that the
+/// face-by-face offset algorithm does not make; its result is then wrong even when it passes the
+/// shape check. \a radius receives the radius of the first such face.
+PartExport bool offsetCollapsesCurvedFace(const TopoDS_Shape& shape, double offset, double& radius);
+
 }  // namespace Part
 #endif  // PART_FEATUREOFFSET_H
